              "id": "1763167094240_1",
              "name": "question",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{\"Only find answer in the provided reference, do not generate your own answers for: \" + $context.$system.$inputMessage}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"title\": \"AnswerWithCitations\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"value\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The answer text.\"\n    },\n    \"citations\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"description\": \"List of citations relevant to the answer.\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"citedText\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"The cited text.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"citedText\"\n        ],\n        \"additionalProperties\": false\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"value\",\n    \"citations\"\n  ],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "RAG_DOCUMENT_TOOL"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Add node for false branch",
            "name": "Add (False Branch)"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1763167909241"
          },
          "id": "add_false_1763166862435",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "ADD"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Present Final Answer"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "PRESENT_FINAL_ANSWER",
          "id": "1763167909241",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1763167909243_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Your task is to answer the user’s question strictly based on the results provided by the tools. Only consider outputs that are **directly relevant** to the user's original query and within the same product/context.  Ignore any unrelated or out-of-scope responses. Ensure your response follows the specified output format exactly.\n\n\nUser question: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \nProduct Public Documentation tool result:  {{$context.$nodes.PRODUCT_PUBLIC_DOCUMENTATION.$output}} \nKnowledgeSearch tool result: {{$context.$nodes.FETCH_FULL_ARTICLE.$output}}, title={{$context.$nodes.GET_BEST_MATCHING_ARTICLE.$output.items[0].title}},  documentId={{$context.$nodes.GET_BEST_MATCHING_ARTICLE.$output.items[0].documentId}}\nInternal Documentation RAG tool result: {{$context.$nodes.INTERNAL_DOCUMENTATION_RAG.$output.value}} \n\n\n# Response Guidelines\n\n**Always deliver enterprise-ready answers that are clear, accurate, and easy to scan at a glance.**\n\n## Core Principles\n- Response must be immediately understandable—fit key info in 1–2 sentences or a concise list.\n- Answers must fit in ≤4 short lines so users never have to scroll to grasp the main point.\n- Begin every response with the key answer or recommendation.\n- Avoid slashes (/) in responses. Replace them with natural connectors like “and,” “or,” “versus,” “with,” “between,” etc.\n- When using the output from Internal Documentation RAG tool, include only the information from the provided references. Do not include any generated content.\n- Only consider tool outputs that directly addresses user's original query/content.\n\n\n## Yes/No Queries\n- **Always start with 'Yes' or 'No'** as the first word.\n- Follow immediately with a brief, direct explanation.\n- If additional supporting facts are critical, use a bulleted or numbered list (max 4 items, ≤15 words per item).\n\n## Non–Yes/No Queries\n- Use one concise sentence (≤20 words) if possible.\n- Only use bullets or numbered lists if steps/options contrast or cannot be expressed in a single sentence.\n- Each bullet/numbered item: ≤15 words. Max 4 bullets.\n- Always lead with the most important fact; details follow.\n\n## Formatting Rules\n- Bullets and numbers are for lists of steps, essential distinctions, or ≥2 independent, short facts.\n- Do not use bullets or numbers by default; only if they improve clarity.\n- Each response must be readable at a glance—never more than 4 single-space lines.\n\n## Style & Content\n- No repetition, filler, speculation, or rephrasing of the user's question.\n- Use official product/enterprise terminology; minimal paraphrasing, always for brevity or clarity.\n- Maintain a neutral, professional, and accessible tone for employees, managers, and HR.\n- Your answer should be based only on the information available to you in the tool calling chat history. You should never invent or make up answers. If no relevant outputs from tools, return exactly: `\"Information not available. Please consult Oracle documentation or support.\"`, **do not** suggest any useful help center article. If the question requires you to synthesize answers across several tool responses, you should do that. Note that some information may need to be summarized from across multiple places in a given object. Use your inference and semantic knowledge to derive the answer from the data without inventing anything.\n\n### ANSWER CONTENT\n- Add citation towards end of the answer.\n  \n#### Rules to generate citation.\n    - If any useful Knowledge article from the KnowledgeSearch tool is used to generate the final answer, include citation in following format: `Useful Knowledge Base article: title – documentId1, documentId2`. Only use documentId, do not use recordId.\n        -  **NEVER** include KM citation if KnowledgeSearch tool generated irrelevant answer.\n    - If any documents from the Product Public Documentation tool are used to generate the final answer, include a link to the original article in the following format: `Useful Help Center article: link`\n        -  **NEVER** include link to original article if Product Public Documentation tool generated irrelevant answer.\n    - Do not generate citations for the Internal Documentation RAG tool, regardless of the answer’s relevance to the user’s query.\n  \n  \n## ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS\n* Do not mention tool calls, chat history, underlying operations, or system processes.\n* Do not include any introductory phrases in final answer.\n* Do not include any Markdown syntax in the final answer.\n* Keep the response natural and conversational without unnecessary preambles.\n* Provide a direct and engaging response without phrases like \"Based on tool calls\" or similar references.\n* Do not append any characters or trailing Periods (.) at the end of valid URLs.\n* If link is generated by DeepLink tool do not remove from response."
            },
            {
              "id": "1763167909243_2",
              "name": "temperature",
              "type": "number"
            }
